## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to reason about cascading failures in a real-world, multi-region microservices architecture. It evaluates understanding of both preventive controls (rate limits, circuit breakers) and reactive strategies (cache bypass, warmup) with measurable SLOs and fast rollback capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Per-endpoint rate limiting and circuit breakers for load control
- Cache warmup and controlled rollouts for spike preparation
- Backpressure and producer throttling to regulate traffic flow
- Eviction tuning and failover paths for resilience
- Automated rollback and SLO-driven incident response

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple token bucket limiter (conceptual)
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, refillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.refillRate = refillRate;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }

  allowRequest() {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= 1) {
      this.tokens -= 1;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.refillRate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable alerting that reduces noise while preserving critical signals, across multi-region K8s clusters, using common tools, with safe rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Alert routing and deduplication (Alertmanager, labels)
- Global blackout policy with per-region windows
- Canary rollout for rule changes; staging validation
- Metrics: alert rate, MTTA, MTTR, missed-incident risk; rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple in-memory alert suppression
const suppression = new Map(); // key -> timestamp until which alerts are muted
function shouldAlert(key) {
  const t = suppression.get(key);
  if (!t) return true;
  return Date.now() > t;
}
function suppress(key, durationMs) {
  suppression.set(key, Date.now() + durationMs);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for cross-cloud regions with drift?
- How would you validate that suppression does not hide critical incidents during outages?

